.TH GBILD 1 gbild
.SH NAME
gbild \- GTK+ 2 Image viewer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gbild
.RB [ \-s \ \fIalgorithm\fP]
.RB [ \-S \ \fIsize\fP]
.RB [ \-C \ \fIcolour1\fP[ : \fIcolour2\fP]]
.RB [ \-z \ \fIzoom\fP]
.RB [ -fpctn ]
.RB [ +fpctnC ]
.RI [ file "] ..."

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gbild
is a GTK+ 2 image viewer.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Start in full-screen mode.
.TP
.B +f
Do not start in full-screen mode.
.TP
.B \-p
Show the property pane.
.TP
.B +p
Hide the property pane.
.TP
.B \-c
Show the image collection.
.TP
.B +c
Hide the image collection.
.TP
.B \-t
Apply an image's embedded orientation.
.TP
.B +t
Do not apply an image's embedded orientation.
.TP
.B \-n
Use the image resolution and display resolution to make normal size a physical size.
.TP
.B +n
Use one source pixel per display pixel for normal size.
.TP
.BI \-s \ algorithm
Set the scaling algorithm. Supported values are
.BR nearest ,
.BR bilinear ,
and
.BR gaussian .
.TP
.BI \-S \ size
Set the chequer square size in pixels. A size of 0 disables the chequered background.
.TP
.BI \-C \ colour1\fR[ : colour2\fR]
Enable the chequered background and set its colours. If the second colour is omitted, the first colour is used for both squares.

Colours use hexadecimal
.IR RGB ,
.IR RRGGBB ,
.IR RRRRGGGGBBBB ,
.IR RGBA ,
.IR RRGGBBAA ,
or
.I RRRRGGGGBBBBAAAA
notation, with an optional
.BR # ,
.BR 0x ,
or
.B 0X
prefix. RGB-only forms may have a leading alpha percentage;
for example,
.B 25%ABCDEF
sets alpha to 25 percent.
.TP
.B +C
Disable the chequered background.
.TP
.BI \-z \ zoom
Set the initial zoom.
.I zoom
shall either be the zoom expressed in perfect (e.g\.\,
.BR 100% )
or ratio (e.g\.\,
.BR 1:1 ),
or one of the following modes:
.RS
.TP
.B width
Fit to width
.TP
.B height
Fit to height
.TP
.B window
Fit to window
.TP
.B best
Best fit
.TP
.B stretch
Stretch to window
.RE

.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file
Image file to open.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The program exited successfully.
.TP
1
An error occurred.

.SH SEE ALSO
None.
